{"hash": "8d99f88ff8f88464", "text": "Some paper sits on the desk every turn. First, the system prompt: the app's own hidden instructions, read before anything you type. Anthropic publishes the ones for its Claude apps. Second, your standing instructions: preferences, styles and project instructions, set once and re-sent every turn. Third, instruction files that load themselves. Put a file called Claude dot M D at the root of a project, and Claude Code reads it at the start of every session there. Your user folder, your company and sub-folders can have one too. Agents dot M D is the open version other tools use, and Claude Code now reads it too, when there's no Claude dot M D. Gemini dot M D and Cursor's rules are the same idea. But a note is not a lock. Hooks and permissions enforce. A long note gets followed less, and it costs tokens every turn. Instruction files get their own lesson in The Machine.", "alignment": {"characters": ["S", "o", "m", "e", " ", "p", "a", "p", "e", "r", " ", "s", "i", "t", "s", " ", "o", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "d", "e", "s", "k", " ", "e", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "t", "u", "r", "n", ".", " ", "F", "i", "r", "s", "t", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "y", "s", "t", "e", "m", " ", "p", "r", "o", "m", "p", "t", ":", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "a", "p", "p", "'", "s", " ", "o", "w", "n", " ", "h", "i", "d", "d", "e", "n", " ", "i", "n", "s", "t", "r", "u", "c", "t", "i", "o", "n", "s", ",", " ", "r", "e", "a", "d", " ", "b", "e", "f", "o", "r", "e", " ", "a", "n", "y", "t", "h", "i", "n", "g", " ", "y", "o", "u", " ", "t", "y", "p", "e", ".", " ", "A", "n", "t", "h", "r", "o", "p", "i", "c", " ", "p", "u", "b", "l", "i", "s", "h", "e", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "o", "n", "e", "s", " ", "f", "o", "r", " ", "i", "t", "s", " ", "C", "l", "a", "u", "d", "e", " ", "a", "p", "p", "s", ".", " ", "S", "e", "c", "o", "n", "d", ",", " ", "y", "o", "u", "r", " ", "s", "t", "a", "n", "d", "i", "n", "g", " ", "i", "n", "s", "t", "r", "u", "c",